1. Root Cause Diagnosis (Duplex Mismatch):
  - late_collisions (412) : Collision detected AFTER transmitting 512 bits (64B slot time);
    signature symptom of Half-Duplex PC receiving simultaneous frames from a Full-Duplex switch.
  - crc_errors (1907)     : Corrupted frames arriving mid-transmission or damaged by EMI.
  - Switch side           : Gigabit switch port set to Auto-negotiation defaults to Half-Duplex when
    parallel-detecting a forced 100M/Half PC, OR switch was forced Full-Duplex while PC is Half.

2. Corrective Configuration Commands:
  Linux   : sudo ethtool -s eth0 speed 1000 duplex full autoneg on
            (verify with: ethtool eth0 && ethtool -S eth0)
  Windows : Set-NetAdapterAdvancedProperty -Name 'Ethernet' -DisplayName 'Speed & Duplex' -DisplayValue 'Auto Negotiation'

3. MAC Address Analysis:
  - 01:00:5e:0a:01:02 -> GROUP (IPv4 Multicast) MAC: LSB of first byte (0x01) is 1,
    and 01:00:5e prefix maps IPv4 multicast (e.g. 224.10.1.2 / 234.10.1.2).
  - 3c:52:82:4e:11:07 -> First 3 bytes (3c:52:82) are the OUI identifying the NIC vendor (HP Inc.).

4. Jumbo Frames (9,000 bytes) for CCTV Storage Server:
  - Benefit: Cuts framing/interrupt overhead (6x fewer headers/IRQs for large sequential video writes).
  - Requirement: End-to-end MTU=9000 must be configured on server NIC, ALL switches in path, and storage NAS;
    otherwise frames are dropped or fragmented.

5. Alternative Concept Analysis: Industrial Switch Ring (MRP/RSTP) vs Star:
  - Ring (IEC 62439-2 MRP / Rapid Ring): Single cable cut recovers in <10-50 ms; ZERO devices lose connection.
  - Star of switches: Cut on uplink disconnects entire downstream switch (~1-30 s only if redundant STP link exists).

